        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": false,
    "closedAt": null,
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Glad you like it so far!\r\n\r\nNo, there is no such functionality and likely won't be at its 100%. The main reason is that this would require keeping track of what files should be considered alternative on per language/filetype basis. Which is highly against 'mini.nvim' principles (except if it brings **considerable** quality of life improvement).\r\n\r\nI wonder if just suggesting files that have same basename without extension inside current file's directoru is enough here?\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Glad you like it so far!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">No, there is no such functionality and likely won't be at its 100%. The main reason is that this would require keeping track of what files should be considered alternative on per language/filetype basis. Which is highly against 'mini.nvim' principles (except if it brings <strong>considerable</strong> quality of life improvement).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I wonder if just suggesting files that have same basename without extension inside current file's directoru is enough here?</p>",
            "bodyText": "Glad you like it so far!\nNo, there is no such functionality and likely won't be at its 100%. The main reason is that this would require keeping track of what files should be considered alternative on per language/filetype basis. Which is highly against 'mini.nvim' principles (except if it brings considerable quality of life improvement).\nI wonder if just suggesting files that have same basename without extension inside current file's directoru is enough here?",
